  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models dominate (0.485–0.653) while image-only is very weak (0.208). The largest single gain so far is multiprofile with scvi_n200 (0.520→0.650, +13 pts), and aggregation (avgpool vs transformer) makes negligible difference. Uncertainty: We do not yet know whether the multiprofile gain is a general property of multi-profile representations or is specific to the learned scvi encoder. Config_002 (pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool) completes a clean 2×2 comparison: it shares the encoder with config_001 (singleprofile, pca, 0.485) to isolate the multiprofile effect, and shares the profile+aggregation with config_005 (scvi, multiprofile, avgpool, 0.650) to isolate the encoder effect under multiprofile. This single experiment simultaneously clarifies whether multiprofile is a universal win and how much of the current performance is attributable to encoder choice vs. profile setting, which directly informs whether to invest further in scgpt encoders, multimodal fusion, or profile/aggregation refinements."
}

